---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Script Library · Both of You" description="Every script from all 20 modules, organised by the moment you're in." current="grow" noindex={true}>

  <div class="scripts-page">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="scripts-header">
      <div class="scripts-nav">
        <a href="/grow/home" class="scripts-back">← Your program</a>
      </div>
      <div class="scripts-label">Both of You</div>
      <h1 class="scripts-title">Script Library</h1>
      <p class="scripts-sub">Every script from all 20 modules, organised by the moment you're in.<br/>Not for the calm morning. For the 5pm Tuesday.</p>

      <a href="/both-of-you-script-library.pdf" download="both-of-you-script-library.pdf" class="scripts-download">
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none">
          <path d="M8 2v8M8 10l-3-3M8 10l3-3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M2 12h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        </svg>
        Download PDF to print
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Sections -->
    <div class="scripts-body">

      <!-- How to use -->
      <div class="scripts-intro">
        <p>These scripts are not lines to memorise. They're starting points. Use the ones that sound like you. Change the words to yours. The goal is a sentence you can actually say when you have nothing left.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- S1: Before you snap -->
      <section class="script-section">
        <div class="script-section-header">
          <div class="script-section-num">1</div>
          <div>
            <h2>Before you snap</h2>
            <p>The signal arrives before the reaction. You have about 30 seconds. This script uses it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-blue">
          <div class="script-when">SAY OUT LOUD · THEN MOVE TO A DIFFERENT ROOM</div>
          <div class="script-text">"I need one second."</div>
          <div class="script-note">Sixty seconds. Not calm, just away from the input that drove you to threshold. Return with fewer words and lower volume. You're not fixing it. You're stopping the amplification.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-neutral">
          <div class="script-when">SAY TO YOURSELF · NOT OUT LOUD</div>
          <div class="script-text script-italic">The cup didn't cause it. The full container caused it.</div>
          <div class="script-note">The trigger is rarely the real trigger. This reframe interrupts the shame spiral by naming what actually happened: the stack, not the spark.</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- S2: When both go under -->
      <section class="script-section">
        <div class="script-section-header">
          <div class="script-section-num">2</div>
          <div>
            <h2>When both of you are in it</h2>
            <p>Two dysregulated nervous systems in the same room amplify each other. The only useful move is to reduce the mutual input.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-blue">
          <div class="script-when">SAY BEFORE LEAVING THE ROOM</div>
          <div class="script-text">"I need a minute. I'll be back."</div>
          <div class="script-note">This sentence names the withdrawal so it doesn't read as abandonment, and promises return. Leave. Sixty seconds minimum. Come back with fewer words, lower volume, no attempt to resolve yet.</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- S3: Argument -->
      <section class="script-section">
        <div class="script-section-header">
          <div class="script-section-num">3</div>
          <div>
            <h2>When the argument won't stop</h2>
            <p>The loop runs because your brain is chasing closure it can't have right now. Every sentence past the third works against you.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-blue">
          <div class="script-when">CHOOSE ONE · SAY IT ONCE · THEN PHYSICALLY MOVE</div>
          <div class="script-text">"We're not talking about this right now."</div>
          <div class="script-text">"My answer isn't changing."</div>
          <div class="script-text">"I've said what I needed to say."</div>
          <div class="script-note">Do not repeat the sentence if they push back. Repeating it is re-entering the loop through a different door. The lesson can be delivered calmly twelve hours later. That version actually lands.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-sage">
          <div class="script-when">12 HOURS LATER · WHEN BOTH OF YOU ARE CALM</div>
          <div class="script-text">"Here's what I was actually trying to say: ___"</div>
          <div class="script-note">Two sentences. The point you were trying to make, delivered in conditions where it can be received. This is not the same conversation. Don't make it the same conversation.</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- S4: Repair -->
      <section class="script-section">
        <div class="script-section-header">
          <div class="script-section-num">4</div>
          <div>
            <h2>After you lost it</h2>
            <p>Two sentences. Delivered when both of you are calm. Not immediately. Before bed is fine. The next morning is fine. Say the two sentences. Then do something ordinary.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-sage">
          <div class="script-when">IF YOU EXPLODED</div>
          <div class="script-text">"I yelled at you this morning and that wasn't okay. I'm going to work on leaving the room before I get that loud."</div>
          <div class="script-note">Sentence one names what happened. Sentence two names what you're going to try. Not a promise, a try. Then stop. Don't add context. Two sentences, then something ordinary.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-sage">
          <div class="script-when">IF YOU SHUT DOWN</div>
          <div class="script-text">"I went quiet and disappeared and that wasn't fair. I'm going to work on coming back sooner instead of waiting until I feel ready."</div>
          <div class="script-note">The withdrawal repair. Names the specific thing that happened, not the explosion. Same structure: what happened, what I'm going to try.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-sage">
          <div class="script-when">IF YOU SAID THE THING</div>
          <div class="script-text">"I said something sharp and I shouldn't have. I'm going to work on stopping before I say the thing I don't mean."</div>
          <div class="script-note">Pick the repair that fits the actual thing that happened, not the most dramatic version of it.</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- S5: Child falling apart -->
      <section class="script-section">
        <div class="script-section-header">
          <div class="script-section-num">5</div>
          <div>
            <h2>When your child is falling apart</h2>
            <p>Their container was already full when they arrived home. The cup wasn't the cause. One sentence, then wait.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-blue">
          <div class="script-when">SAY ONCE · THEN WAIT 30 SECONDS BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE</div>
          <div class="script-text">"That's really upsetting you."</div>
          <div class="script-note">Not "it's fine." Not "it's just a biscuit." Just acknowledgment, then silence. No evaluation of whether the upset is proportionate. The peak always passes. Your job during the peak is to not add input.</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- S6: Checked out -->
      <section class="script-section">
        <div class="script-section-header">
          <div class="script-section-num">6</div>
          <div>
            <h2>When you've checked out</h2>
            <p>You don't regulate first and then return. You return, and that's what starts the regulation.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-blue">
          <div class="script-when">NAME IT BEFORE YOU GO</div>
          <div class="script-text">"I need five minutes. I'll be back."</div>
          <div class="script-note">Named withdrawals are workable. Unnamed ones leave a gap that fills with your child's interpretation, usually something about themselves.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-neutral">
          <div class="script-when">WHEN YOU RETURN · PICK ONE</div>
          <div class="script-text">"I needed a minute. I'm back."</div>
          <div class="script-text">"Do you want some water?"</div>
          <div class="script-or">or sit near them for 30 seconds without speaking</div>
          <div class="script-note">Physical presence is the regulating event, not the readiness that precedes it. Small enough to do when you have nothing left is the only design specification that matters.</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- S7: Partner -->
      <section class="script-section">
        <div class="script-section-header">
          <div class="script-section-num">7</div>
          <div>
            <h2>For the partner conversation</h2>
            <p>They see the match. They don't see what was already burning. The goal isn't one agreed version. It's understanding there were two.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-lavender">
          <div class="script-when">START HERE · THEN ACTUALLY LISTEN TO THE FULL ANSWER</div>
          <div class="script-text">"What did you see happening just before it went wrong?"</div>
          <div class="script-note">Their answer will be different from yours. Both are real. Don't interrupt to correct. The conversation is about building two versions, not one.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-lavender">
          <div class="script-when">THEN ADD YOUR VERSION · AS INFORMATION, NOT A DEFENCE</div>
          <div class="script-text">"I hear what you saw. What I was managing before that moment was ___."</div>
          <div class="script-note">"I hear what you saw" signals that you received their account before contributing yours. That order matters.</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- S8: School -->
      <section class="script-section">
        <div class="script-section-header">
          <div class="script-section-num">8</div>
          <div>
            <h2>For the school conversation</h2>
            <p>You're adding a layer of information to their picture of your child, not asking them to change their version.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-neutral">
          <div class="script-when">OPENING THE CONTEXT CONVERSATION</div>
          <div class="script-text">"I understand what you observed. I want to give you some context about what was happening for them before that moment."</div>
          <div class="script-note">Then one piece of specific, recent context. Not a defence. An explanation of the cause. Something the school can actually use. Over time, that layer accumulates.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-neutral">
          <div class="script-when">WHEN YOU THINK SOMETHING ELSE MAY ALSO BE PRESENT</div>
          <div class="script-text">"There's something I've been noticing about [name] that doesn't quite fit the ADHD picture. Can I describe it and get your thoughts?"</div>
          <div class="script-note">Not a diagnostic label. An observation in specific behavioural terms. That's enough to open the conversation.</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- S9: Internal -->
      <section class="script-section">
        <div class="script-section-header">
          <div class="script-section-num">9</div>
          <div>
            <h2>The internal script</h2>
            <p>What to say to yourself, not out loud. Not affirmations. Structural reframes that interrupt the shame spiral before it has momentum.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-red">
          <div class="script-when">WHEN THE GAP BETWEEN KNOWING AND DOING OPENS UP</div>
          <div class="script-text script-italic">I know what I'm supposed to do. I couldn't do it right now. That's the thing I'm working on.</div>
          <div class="script-note">The gap is not a character flaw. It's what happens when the tools don't fit the conditions. The reframe is the first action.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-red">
          <div class="script-when">WHEN THE SHAME ARRIVES</div>
          <div class="script-text script-italic">This is structural, not personal.</div>
          <div class="script-note">You've been applying tools designed for a different nervous system configuration. That's a design mismatch. Structural problems have structural solutions.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-red">
          <div class="script-when">WHEN THE SPIRAL IS RUNNING</div>
          <div class="script-text script-italic">I've already counted that. I don't need to count it again.</div>
          <div class="script-note">Rumination is a search for resolution that isn't available inside the spiral. This gives you a foothold when you notice you're three laps in.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="script-card script-card-red">
          <div class="script-when">ON THE HARD DAYS</div>
          <div class="script-text script-italic">Slightly earlier. Not perfectly. Not always.</div>
          <div class="script-note">This is the whole goal. One notch upstream of where you were before. That's real progress, even when it doesn't look like it.</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Download repeat -->
      <div class="scripts-download-footer">
        <a href="/both-of-you-script-library.pdf" download="both-of-you-script-library.pdf" class="scripts-download">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none">
            <path d="M8 2v8M8 10l-3-3M8 10l3-3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            <path d="M2 12h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
          Download PDF to print
        </a>
        <p class="scripts-download-note">Print it. Put it where you'll see it before you need to remember it.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

</Base>

<style>
.scripts-page {
  max-width: 680px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 var(--page-pad) 80px;
}
.scripts-nav {
  padding: var(--space-xl) 0 0;
}
.scripts-back {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  color: var(--pewter);
  text-decoration: none;
}
.scripts-header {
  padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--mist-border);
  margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
}
.scripts-label {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 9px;
  letter-spacing: 0.2em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--blue);
  margin: var(--space-xl) 0 var(--space-sm);
}
.scripts-title {
  font-family: var(--serif);
  font-size: clamp(28px, 6vw, 42px);
  font-weight: 300;
  color: var(--slate);
  font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 44;
  line-height: 1.15;
  margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
}
.scripts-sub {
  font-family: var(--sans);
  font-size: 16px;
  color: var(--pewter);
  line-height: 1.6;
  margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
}
.scripts-download {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--blue);
  background: rgba(74,111,165,0.06);
  border: 1px solid rgba(74,111,165,0.25);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  padding: 10px 16px;
  text-decoration: none;
  transition: background 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
}
.scripts-download:hover {
  background: rgba(74,111,165,0.12);
  border-color: rgba(74,111,165,0.4);
}
.scripts-intro {
  margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
}
.scripts-intro p {
  font-family: var(--sans);
  font-size: 15px;
  color: var(--pewter);
  line-height: 1.7;
}

/* Section */
.script-section {
  margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
}
.script-section-header {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 16px;
  margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
}
.script-section-num {
  font-family: var(--serif);
  font-size: 32px;
  font-weight: 300;
  color: var(--blue);
  font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 36;
  line-height: 1;
  flex-shrink: 0;
  width: 36px;
  padding-top: 2px;
}
.script-section-header h2 {
  font-family: var(--serif);
  font-size: 20px;
  font-weight: 400;
  color: var(--slate);
  font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 24;
  line-height: 1.25;
  margin-bottom: 4px;
}
.script-section-header p {
  font-family: var(--sans);
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--pewter);
  line-height: 1.55;
}

/* Cards */
.script-card {
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 18px 20px;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}
.script-card-blue  { background: rgba(74,111,165,0.07);  border: 1.5px solid rgba(74,111,165,0.25); }
.script-card-sage  { background: rgba(168,195,160,0.12); border: 1.5px solid rgba(168,195,160,0.4); }
.script-card-neutral { background: rgba(31,42,55,0.03);  border: 1.5px solid rgba(31,42,55,0.1); }
.script-card-lavender { background: rgba(155,139,180,0.08); border: 1.5px solid rgba(155,139,180,0.3); }
.script-card-red   { background: rgba(201,123,106,0.07); border: 1.5px solid rgba(201,123,106,0.25); }

.script-when {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 8.5px;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--pewter);
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
.script-text {
  font-family: var(--sans);
  font-size: 17px;
  color: var(--slate);
  line-height: 1.55;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
  font-weight: 400;
}
.script-italic {
  font-style: italic;
  color: var(--slate);
}
.script-or {
  font-family: var(--sans);
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--pewter);
  font-style: italic;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
  padding-left: 2px;
}
.script-note {
  font-family: var(--sans);
  font-size: 12px;
  color: var(--pewter);
  line-height: 1.6;
  border-top: 1px solid rgba(31,42,55,0.08);
  padding-top: 10px;
  margin-top: 10px;
}

.scripts-download-footer {
  padding-top: var(--space-2xl);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--mist-border);
  text-align: center;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
}
.scripts-download-note {
  font-family: var(--sans);
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--pewter);
}
</style>
